exports[`renderBlueprint network gcp on gitlab: the stack's own files 1`] = `
"# infra/staging/main-network/README.md
# staging-main-network

Written by the platform from a blueprint: a \`network\` on \`gcp\`, profile \`small\`.

- \`stack.yml\` marks this directory as a stack: its name, the Terraform version and where the state lives.
- \`main.tf\` sets the provider, calls the module with the values the blueprint allows and passes on the module's public outputs (its console link, and a service's address). It holds no secret.
- The module is a copy at \`../../_blueprints/gcp/network-v1\`, shared by every \`network\` on \`gcp\` in this repository. It is never edited in place: a newer version is a new directory and a new proposal.

Uses nothing.

Change this resource by proposing a change through the platform. A hand edit of these files is overwritten by the next one.

# infra/staging/main-network/main.tf
terraform {
  backend "http" {}
}

provider "google" {
  project = "my-proj-123"
  region  = "us-central1"
}

module "this" {
  source      = "../../_blueprints/gcp/network-v1"
  environment = "staging"
  name        = "main"
  project     = "my-proj-123"
  region      = "us-central1"
  cidr        = "10.20.0.0/16"
}

output "console_url" {
  value = module.this.console_url
}

# infra/staging/main-network/stack.yml
# Written by the platform from a blueprint (network on gcp); see README.md.
name: staging-main-network
tool: terraform
version: 1.5.7
state: gitlab
watch:
  - infra/_blueprints/gcp/network-v1/**
"
`;

