"# infra/staging/main-service/README.md
# staging-main-service

Written by the platform from a blueprint: a \`service\` on \`aws\`, profile \`large\`.

- \`stack.yml\` marks this directory as a stack: its name, the Terraform version and where the state lives.
- \`main.tf\` sets the provider, calls the module with the values the blueprint allows and passes on the module's public outputs (its console link, and a service's address). It holds no secret.
- The module is a copy at \`../../_blueprints/aws/service-v2\`, shared by every \`service\` on \`aws\` in this repository. It is never edited in place: a newer version is a new directory and a new proposal.

Uses: \`bucket:files\`, \`network:main\`, \`postgres:main\`.

Change this resource by proposing a change through the platform. A hand edit of these files is overwritten by the next one.

# infra/staging/main-service/main.tf
terraform {
  backend "http" {}
}

provider "aws" {
  region = "eu-west-2"
}

module "this" {
  source          = "../../_blueprints/aws/service-v2"
  environment     = "staging"
  name            = "main"
  region          = "eu-west-2"
  network         = "main"
  certificate_arn = "arn:aws:acm:eu-west-2:123456789012:certificate/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"
  port            = 8080
  public          = false
  cpu             = 1024
  memory          = 2048
  desired_count   = 3
  databases       = ["main"]
  buckets         = ["files"]
}

output "url" {
  value = module.this.url
}

output "console_url" {
  value = module.this.console_url
}

# infra/staging/main-service/stack.yml
# Written by the platform from a blueprint (service on aws); see README.md.
